All the files are simulated and Implemented using VIVADO. The XDC/UCF file is not attatched. This verilog programs are compatible with both VIVADO and Xilinx
This Simulation exhibits "SMART STREET LIGHT AND TRAFFIC LIGHT CONTROLLER"developed using Verilog HDL and implemented on the Xilinx Spartan-7 (XC7S50CSGA324-2) FPGA platform. Things get very interesting when everything is in nano & µ.
 
 💡 Project Highlights

 ✅ Smart Street Light Controller with adaptive brightness control
 ✅ Day/Night Detection Logic
 ✅ Vehicle Detection-Based Energy Optimization
 ✅ Pedestrian Crossing Management System
 ✅ Traffic Light Controller Integration
 ✅ PWM-Based LED Brightness Control

 💠 Development Flow
🔹 RTL Design in Verilog HDL 
🔹 Functional Simulation and Waveform Verification in Vivado
🔹 RTL Schematic Generation and Hierarchical Design Analysis
🔹 Synthesis and Implementation on Spartan-7 FPGA
🔹 Resource Utilization and Floorplanning Verification

💠 Modules Implemented
➡️ Clock Divider
➡️ Smart Street Light Controller
➡️ PWM Controller
➡️ Traffic Light Controller
➡️ Pedestrian Controller
➡️ Top-Level System Integration

The screenshots showcase:
 🔹 Behavioral Simulation Results
 🔹 RTL Schematic Architecture
 🔹 FPGA Device Implementation and Placement

This project demonstrates how FPGA technology can be leveraged to create energy-efficient smart city infrastructure, combining intelligent lighting, traffic control, and pedestrian safety into a single hardware platform.
